### 1. Sign up (should give 201 Created)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "test1@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "phone": "9876543210",
  "dateOfBirth": "2003-05-17",
  "pan": "ABCDE1234F"
}

### 2. Same email again (should give 409 ALREADY_EXISTS)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Someone Else",
  "email": "test1@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "dateOfBirth": "2001-01-01",
  "pan": "ZZZZZ9999Z"
}

### 3. Bad PAN and bad email (should give 400 INVALID_INPUT)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad Data",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "password123",
  "dateOfBirth": "2001-01-01",
  "pan": "12345"
}

### 4. Under 18 (should give 400 INVALID_INPUT)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Young User",
  "email": "young@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "dateOfBirth": "2012-01-01",
  "pan": "YOUNG1234Y"
}

### 5. Me without login (should give 401)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/me

### 6. Wrong password (should give 401 "Invalid email or password")
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "test1@example.com", "password": "wrongpassword" }

### 7. Login (should give 200 with balance)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "test1@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### 8. Me after login (should give 200, same balance)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/me

### 9. Logout (should give 204)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout

### 10. Me after logout (should give 401 again)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/me

### 11. All quotes (log in first)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/quotes

### 12. One quote
GET http://localhost:8080/api/quotes/RELIANCE